"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"FxyGTyC98dVsVMhPiHXyOQ","review_id":"dyMH6UdnEo4PqnsIv7dFjw","date":"2013-01-24T02:14:49","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.940667450428009,"text_excerpt":"I think you have to be from New Orleans, many moons ago, to understand the demand and desire of New Orleanians and buttermilk drops! There was a bakery called McKenzie's that made some of the best donuts in the state, if not the best, and their buttermilk drops was a hot seller and delicious. They closed down...do to various health violation reasons, but the desire for those buttermilk drops still remains. Everyone claims to have a recipe close to them, or have their recipe overall, but very few people can make that claim once their product is bitten. Then this place jumped up to the plate. EVERY NEW ORLEANIAN has stated that these people have the recipe correct. Those buttermilk drops ar..."},{"business_id":"FxyGTyC98dVsVMhPiHXyOQ","review_id":"7Jiu8ttpR0ugqVbQEDH9CA","date":"2013-03-02T21:41:13","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.93452388048172,"text_excerpt":"Sweet lord are these doughnuts delicious! This place is a trek if you are in a typical tourist locale (French Quarter, etc.) and is most easily accessible by car. The place looks pretty shady, but who cares? They're super friendly and have amazing pastries. The eponymous buttermilk drops are giant cakey bits of wonderful covered in glaze. The doughnuts, fritters, and bear claws are also top notch. If I lived anywhere near here, I would roughly double in size. Go here. Eat. Be happy."},{"business_id":"FxyGTyC98dVsVMhPiHXyOQ","review_id":"iU6OJscFPnGgg9rxjJFNCQ","date":"2021-05-18T23:09:55","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.925620973110199,"text_excerpt":"I'm a big donut lover, and The Buttermilk Drop has really good donuts. It's a local, Black-owned, hole-in-the-wall establishment that is known for its buttermilk drop cake donuts. They also have regular glazed donuts, as well as some varieties of filled donuts (lemon curd, jam, vanilla cream). My favourites are the vanilla cream-filled ones! I also like the buttermilk drop ones (super moist on the inside), but I find them to be a bit greasy at times. Also, their sizes can be inconsistent, too. Overall, it's a great spot for donuts, particularly if you're already in the area."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"FxyGTyC98dVsVMhPiHXyOQ","photo_id":"HmDem3aulhvc8ZCyKWHgEQ","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/HmDem3aulhvc8ZCyKWHgEQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8538868427276611},{"business_id":"FxyGTyC98dVsVMhPiHXyOQ","photo_id":"3AYd-wbbMdWUf9tev8QCnQ","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/3AYd-wbbMdWUf9tev8QCnQ.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8095477819442749},{"business_id":"FxyGTyC98dVsVMhPiHXyOQ","photo_id":"qimZlphiXAIQxrJQkGepfA","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/qimZlphiXAIQxrJQkGepfA.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7771018743515015},{"business_id":"FxyGTyC98dVsVMhPiHXyOQ","photo_id":"Yi1pFHZaMUSQgZZ3_HUEkg","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/Yi1pFHZaMUSQgZZ3_HUEkg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7740167379379272},{"business_id":"FxyGTyC98dVsVMhPiHXyOQ","photo_id":"h3YTssMlgGsJg-ukn4tj9w","label":"outside","image_url":"/photos/h3YTssMlgGsJg-ukn4tj9w.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.7540206909179688}]},"notebook_case":null}
